# fixedbugs, defect 338, lane b11-misc, 2026-10-05.
#
# SYMPTOM: zeros before a base's marker were offered one zero whatever followed
# the marker, so `00x` and `00xg` were offered `0x` and `0xg`, a literal with no
# digits and one with a digit no hexadecimal number has, both refused.
#
# CAUSE: the advice read the one character after the zeros, the marker, and
# never what followed it.
#
# FIX: one zero is offered only where it writes a literal the scanner accepts
# (`leading_zeros.based_literal`, held to the scanner by `number.hero`'s
# test); elsewhere a note says why none is, and how such a literal is written.
# The form is the full one, since the brief form shows no fix.

function main()
    a = 00x    #~ leading_zero
    b = 00xg    #~ leading_zero
    c = 00x7    #~ leading_zero
    print(a, b, c)
